  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "What A Document Actually Is",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A document is an ordered set of field/value pairs — MongoDB's unit of storage. Like a row, but self-describing and nested."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ _id: 1, name: \"Ada\",",
            "  langs: [\"js\", \"go\"],        // array",
            "  addr: { city: \"Dublin\" } }  // subdoc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Documents Live",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "database",
              "collection",
              "document",
              "field/value"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No schema is enforced by default",
            "Two docs in one collection may share no fields",
            "Adding a field is per-document, not a migration",
            "Field order is preserved and returned as inserted",
            "JSON key order in most languages is not"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Self-Describing Cost",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every field name is stored in every document",
            "Short names save real disk and RAM",
            "`txId` beats `transactionIdentifier` at scale"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Field Name Rules",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Empty field names are illegal in most contexts",
            "`$` prefix and `.` legal since 5.0, still risky",
            "They break query and update expressions",
            "Duplicate keys are representable, mostly server-rejected"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Atomic Writes, Bounded Depth"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One insert, update or delete is all-or-nothing",
            "Atomicity holds across nested arrays too",
            "Max nesting depth is 100 levels",
            "Past it: `BSONObj exceeded maximum nested object depth`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Opting Back Into Schema",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.createCollection(\"users\", {",
            "  validator: { $jsonSchema: { /*...*/ } },",
            "  validationLevel: \"strict\",  // or moderate",
            "  validationAction: \"error\"   // or warn",
            "})"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Relational",
                "lines": [
                  "customer + orders + items",
                  "3 tables",
                  "2 joins per read"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Document",
                "lines": [
                  "one entity, one shape",
                  "1 document",
                  "1 read"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "Object.bsonsize({ a: 1 })  // exact bytes",
            "db.c.find().forEach(d =>",
            "  print(Object.bsonsize(d)))"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "BSON: The Binary Encoding",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.posts.updateOne({ _id: p },",
            "  { $inc: { commentCount: 1 } })",
            "// beats recomputing on every read"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Locality Is The Promise",
          "text": "Data accessed together is stored together, so one disk read serves a whole entity."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Binary JSON, Not Text",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "BSON is the real on-disk and on-the-wire format",
            "JSON is only the display layer",
            "Goals: lightweight, traversable, efficient",
            "Fixed-width numeric types are C-friendly"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "matrix",
          "spec": {
            "rows": [
              [
                "int32 length",
                "type byte"
              ],
              [
                "name + 0x00",
                "value"
              ],
              [
                "...",
                "0x00 end"
              ]
            ],
            "highlight": [],
            "caption": "one BSON document"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Element = type byte + cstring name + value",
            "The length prefix lets a parser skip a subdoc",
            "No scanning for a closing brace",
            "Integers little-endian; strings UTF-8, int32 len, null"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Type Codes To Know",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Type",
            "Code",
            "Type"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "0x01",
              "double",
              "0x08",
              "bool"
            ],
            [
              "0x02",
              "string",
              "0x09",
              "utc date"
            ],
            [
              "0x03",
              "subdoc",
              "0x10",
              "int32"
            ],
            [
              "0x04",
              "array",
              "0x12",
              "int64"
            ],
            [
              "0x07",
              "ObjectId",
              "0x13",
              "decimal128"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Types JSON Lacks"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "ObjectId, Date, Binary, Decimal128",
            "Regex, Timestamp, MinKey/MaxKey",
            "Distinct int32, int64 and double",
            "Bigger than JSON for short data: prefixes, type bytes",
            "Smaller for numbers: binary, not decimal text"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Arrays Are Secretly Documents",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// [\"a\", \"b\"] is encoded as",
            "{ \"0\": \"a\", \"1\": \"b\" }   // string keys",
            "// 1M elements = 1M index strings"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading Real Bytes",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "// { a: NumberInt(1) } on the wire",
            "0C 00 00 00   // length = 12",
            "10 61 00      // int32, \"a\\0\"",
            "01 00 00 00   // value 1",
            "00            // end of document"
          ],
          "note": "length counts itself and terminator"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Length `0C 00 00 00` is ==little-endian== 12",
            "Type `0x10` then the cstring name `a\\0`",
            "Value is 4 fixed bytes, then `0x00` closes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Overhead Wins Small",
          "text": "JSON text `{\"a\":1}` is 7 bytes; its BSON is **12** — prefixes and type bytes dominate tiny docs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Extended JSON & Numeric Types",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Index keys are stored as strings, one per element",
            "A million-element array pays that a million times",
            "Huge arrays are costly to store and to update"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Extended JSON",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// canonical (lossless)",
            "{ \"n\": { \"$numberLong\": \"42\" } }",
            "// relaxed (readable)",
            "{ \"n\": 42 }   // mongoexport emits ExtJSON"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Renaming Pays",
          "text": "Shortening one long field name across millions of documents shrinks a collection measurably."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Numbers",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Code",
            "Mint it"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "double",
              "1",
              "shell default"
            ],
            [
              "int32",
              "16",
              "`NumberInt(5)`"
            ],
            [
              "int64",
              "18",
              "`NumberLong(\"5\")`"
            ],
            [
              "decimal128",
              "19",
              "`NumberDecimal(\"9.99\")`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Decimal128 is 128-bit IEEE 754-2008, 34 digits",
            "The only correct type for money",
            "All numeric types compare and sort together",
            "`NumberInt(5)`, `5.0` and `NumberDecimal(\"5\")` all match `5`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Text, Blobs, Structure",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "String (2): UTF-8 only, invalid bytes rejected",
            "String length is bytes, not characters",
            "Object (3) and Array (4): nested up to 100 deep",
            "BinData (5): raw bytes plus a subtype byte"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Subtype",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "0x00",
              "generic bytes"
            ],
            [
              "0x04",
              "UUID"
            ],
            [
              "0x07",
              "compressed time series"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Store hashes, thumbnails, encrypted blobs as BinData",
            "ObjectId (7): 12 bytes, the default `_id` type",
            "Boolean (8) and Null (10) are plain",
            "Undefined (6) is deprecated — drivers send null"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Dates, Sort Order & The _id Field",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Time And Patterns"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Date (9): signed int64 ms since the Unix epoch, UTC",
            "No timezone is stored — the client applies one",
            "Regex (11): pattern plus flags, used by `$regex`",
            "Timestamp (17): internal replication, seconds + ordinal",
            "Never use Timestamp for app time — use Date"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Sort Sentinels",
          "items": [
            "MinKey (-1) compares below every type",
            "MaxKey (127) compares above every type",
            "Handy as open-ended range bounds"
          ],
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Comparison Order",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "MinKey < Null < Numbers < String < Object",
            "Array < BinData < ObjectId < Boolean",
            "Date < Timestamp < Regex < MaxKey",
            "Comparison is type-bracketed, low to high"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Querying By Type"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.c.find({ qty: { $type: \"int\" } })",
            "db.c.find({ qty: { $type: 16 } })  // same",
            "db.c.find({ qty: { $type: \"number\" } })",
            "// number = double|int|long|decimal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Type Is Data",
          "text": "The stored type is part of the value. Choose it at insert time, because you cannot fix it at query time."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Mandatory Primary Key",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every document must have an `_id`",
            "Omit it and the driver mints an ObjectId pre-insert",
            "Unique index `_id_` is mandatory and undroppable",
            "`_id` is immutable — you cannot `$set` it",
            "Changing identity means delete plus reinsert"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Legal `_id` Types",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Any BSON type except an array",
            "Arrays banned: a multikey index breaks uniqueness",
            "A subdocument is allowed",
            "But then field order decides equality"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// these are DIFFERENT _id values",
            "{ _id: { a: 1, b: 2 } }",
            "{ _id: { b: 2, a: 1 } }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Custom Keys Pay Off"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Natural keys: email, SKU, ISO date bucket",
            "A free unique constraint, one less index",
            "Fewer index writes, smaller collection"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.rates.insertOne({",
            "  _id: \"2026-09-07/EURUSD\",  // natural key",
            "  rate: 1.09",
            "})"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "_id Uniqueness & ObjectId Anatomy",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Duplicates And Upserts",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A duplicate raises `E11000 duplicate key error`",
            "Often the intended idempotency guard for retried writes",
            "`_id` always comes back unless you suppress it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.c.find({}, { _id: 0, name: 1 })  // hide it",
            "db.c.updateOne({ _id: k },",
            "  { $set: { qty: 3 } },",
            "  { upsert: true })   // insert or merge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sharding Caveats",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Globally unique only if `_id` is the shard key",
            "Or a prefix of it — otherwise uniqueness is per-shard",
            "A monotonic `_id` shard key hot-spots one shard",
            "Use hashed sharding or a compound key instead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "The Oplog Speaks _id",
          "text": "Single-document reads route by `_id`, and every oplog entry names the documents it changed by `_id`."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "An ObjectId is exactly 12 bytes, rendered as 24 hex characters: `ObjectId(\"65f1a3b4c2d1e0f9a8b7c6d5\")`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Twelve Bytes, Three Fields",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "ts b0",
              "ts b1",
              "ts b2",
              "ts b3",
              "random x5",
              "counter x3"
            ],
            "indices": true,
            "pointers": [],
            "highlight": [],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "12-byte ObjectId"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "4-byte big-endian seconds since the epoch",
            "5-byte random value, one per process",
            "3-byte counter starting at a random value",
            "Old 3-byte machine + 2-byte PID died in 3.4 drivers",
            "Do not parse it for host information"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Time Comes First",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Timestamp leads, so ids sort roughly by creation",
            "`_id` sort approximates creation order to the second",
            "A separate `createdAt` is often redundant"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "oid.getTimestamp()   // -> Date",
            "const lo = ObjectId.createFromTime(",
            "  new Date(\"2026-01-01\") / 1000)",
            "db.c.find({ _id: { $gte: lo } })"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "ObjectId Trade-offs & The 16 MB Cap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Client-Side Minting"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The driver generates it, not the server",
            "No round trip to learn an insert's own id",
            "Many clients stay unique with zero coordination",
            "Uniqueness is probabilistic but strong",
            "A clash needs same second, same random, counter collision"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Size Comparison",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Id form",
            "Bytes",
            "Ordered"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ObjectId",
              "12",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "UUID string",
              "36",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "UUID BinData 4",
              "16",
              "no"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where It Bites",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Ordered ids land at the B-tree right edge: write locality",
            "The same property makes a poor shard key",
            "Public URLs leak creation time and rough counts",
            "Use an opaque public id when that matters"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "ObjectId()               // mint a new one",
            "ObjectId(\"65f1a3b4...\")  // parse a hex string",
            "db.c.find({ _id: \"65f1a3b4...\" })",
            "// matches NOTHING — string is not ObjectId"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Types Must Match Exactly",
          "text": "A 24-hex string never matches an ObjectId. Cast at the edge of your application, every time."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "A Hard Ceiling",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "16 MiB = 16,777,216 bytes per document",
            "A server limit, not a tunable",
            "Measured as encoded BSON, not JSON text",
            "Field names, type bytes and length prefixes all count"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why The Cap Exists",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bounds per-document RAM use",
            "Stops one document monopolising bandwidth",
            "Keeps working-set behaviour predictable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where It Applies"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Documents at rest",
            "Replacement documents and update results",
            "Intermediate aggregation results",
            "Each pipeline stage's output document"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "Object.bsonsize(db.c.findOne({ _id: x }))",
            "// -> 4194304   true encoded size",
            "// check before you push more in"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Outgrowing 16 MB & Embedding Subdocuments",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How It Actually Fails",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Unbounded arrays creep up: comments, events, log lines",
            "Then writes simply start failing",
            "`BSONObjectTooLarge`",
            "`Resulting document after update is larger than 16777216`",
            "`$group` with `$push` on high cardinality blows up the same"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "A Different Limit, Do Not Confuse",
          "items": [
            "Pipeline memory per stage caps at 100 MB",
            "`allowDiskUse: true` lifts that for `$sort`/`$group`",
            "It does NOT lift the 16 MB document cap"
          ],
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Room For Big Data"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Option",
            "How it works"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "GridFS",
              "255 KB chunks + `fs.files`"
            ],
            [
              "Object store",
              "URL, size, checksum only"
            ],
            [
              "Bucket",
              "doc per device-hour, capped"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ device: \"d1\", hour: \"2026-09-07T14\",",
            "  count: 58,            // roll at N",
            "  readings: [ /* <= 200 */ ] }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Long Before 16 MB",
          "text": "If a document routinely passes a few hundred KB, the data model is already wrong."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Embedding nests related data straight inside the parent, as a subdocument or an array of subdocuments."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ _id: 7, total: 42,",
            "  items: [ { sku: \"A1\", qty: 2 },",
            "           { sku: \"B2\", qty: 1 } ] }",
            "// one find() returns the whole order"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reaching Inside",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.u.find({ \"addr.city\": \"Dublin\" })",
            "db.u.createIndex({ \"addr.city\": 1 })",
            "db.u.find({ addr:",
            "  { city: \"Dublin\", zip: \"D2\" } })  // exact"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Dot notation queries and indexes nested fields",
            "Whole-subdocument equality needs exact fields and order",
            "`$elemMatch` makes one element satisfy all conditions",
            "Without it, two conditions can match two elements"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.s.find({ scores: { $elemMatch: {",
            "  s: { $gt: 80 }, subj: \"math\" } } })",
            "// one element must clear both"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Updating Array Elements",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Operator",
            "Hits"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`$`",
              "first match"
            ],
            [
              "`$[]`",
              "every element"
            ],
            [
              "`$[t]`",
              "`arrayFilters` match"
            ]
          ]
        }
